message.content:
Sure! Below is a minimal example of an “interactive rotating card” that flips when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file and open it in your browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣ Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body {
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    min-height:100vh;
    margin:0;
    background:#f0f0f0;
    font-family:sans-serif;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣ Card container (perspective) ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
    perspective:800px;          /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣ Card itself (front + back) ---------- */
.card {
    width:260px;
    height:360px;
    position:relative;
    cursor:pointer;
    transition:transform .6s ease-in-out;
    transform-style:preserve-3d;   /* keep children in 3D space */
}

.card:hover {                     /* rotate on hover */
    transform:rotateY(180deg);     /* Y‑axis flip – change to X for vertical flip */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣ Front side ---------- */
.front,
.back {
    position:absolute;
    inset:0;                      /* top/right/bottom/left all set to 0 */
    backface-visibility:hidden;   /* hide backside while flipping */
    border-radius:12px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,.25);
}

.front {
    background:#fff;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

.front img {
    max-width:100%;
    border-radius:8px;
    margin-bottom:15px;
}

.front h3 {
    margin:0 0 10px;
    color:#333;
}
.front p {
    color:#666;
    line-height:1.5;
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣ Back side ---------- */
.back {
    background:#fafafa;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);      /* start rotated so it's hidden initially */
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

.back h3 {
    margin:0 0 10px;
    color:#444;
}
.back p {
    color:#555;
    line-height:1.5;
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front -->
        <div class="front">
            <img src="https://picsum.photos/260/200?random=1" alt="Random image">
            <h3>Tytuł karty</h3>
            <p>To jest przykładowy opis frontu karty.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Back -->
        <div class="back">
            <h3>Backside Title</h3>
            <p>Treść z tyłu karty pojawia się po obróceniu.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| **1** | `perspective` on the wrapper creates a 3D context. |
| **2** | `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps child elements in 3D space. |
| **3** | `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the reverse side during rotation. |
| **4** | On hover we apply `transform: rotateY(180deg)` to the whole card. |
| **5** | The back side is pre‑rotated (`rotateY(180deg)`) so it becomes visible after the flip. |

#### Customization tips

- Change `rotateY` to `rotateX` if you prefer a vertical flip.
- Adjust `perspective` value for stronger/weaker depth.
- Add more content or style the card with gradients, shadows, etc.

Happy coding!
